program's licence neither grants nor restricts anything about the weights.

The restrictions below are the publishers'. They are reproduced here because
they are easy to miss and they bind the person running the app, not its author.

  MiniMax H3 (MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3)
    MiniMax H3 Community License.
      - Restricts use in the USA, the EU, the UK and South Korea.
      - Requires authorisation above roughly US$20M revenue.
      - Prohibits training other models on H3 output.
      - Prohibits unlawful and pornographic output, in any territory.
    There is no server-side filter on a local run. Complying is your
    responsibility. The app asks you to acknowledge this on first launch.

  Community and third-party checkpoints
    Quantized conversions, turbo LoRAs and alternative text encoders each carry
    their own terms, which are often unstated. Where a licence is unclear, the
    catalogue marks the entry as community provenance; read the model card
    before relying on it for anything that matters.

Running this app in the USA, the EU, the UK or South Korea is not in itself a
problem — the restriction is on the weights, not the software.


